1. Definitions

   "Project Cobalt" means the framework of that name published at
   https://github.com/Project-Cobalt-FiveM.

   "Derivative" means any work that contains the Software, in whole or in
   part, modified or not, including translations, ports and resources
   built by changing the Software's code.

   "Server" means a FiveM, RedM or similar game server.

2. What you may do

   Subject to the conditions below, you may, free of charge:

   a. use and run the Software, or a Derivative, on any number of Servers;
   b. run those Servers commercially, including taking donations, selling
      in-game perks, ranks, priority queue or other server benefits, and
      charging for access to the Server;
   c. study and modify the Software for your own use;
   d. share the Software and Derivatives under the conditions in section 3;
   e. charge for your own services around the Software, such as hosting,
      installation, configuration or custom development, as long as the
      Software and any Derivative itself is handed over under this license
      at no extra cost.

3. Conditions

   a. Source stays open. If you share the Software or a Derivative with
      anyone outside your own team, in any form, you must make its complete,
      readable source code available to them under this same license, at
      no charge. You may not obfuscate, encrypt or escrow it, including
      through FiveM Asset Escrow, or ship it only in a form that hides the
      source.

   b. No selling the code. You may not sell, resell, rent, sublicense for a
      fee or otherwise charge for the Software or a Derivative itself,
      whether on Tebex, a store, a marketplace, a paid Discord, a
      subscription or any other paid channel, alone or bundled with other
      products. Section 2e describes the services you may charge for.

   c. The name stays. The Software must stay identified as part of Project
      Cobalt. You may not rename, rebrand or present the Software or a
      Derivative as a different framework or product. Resource names keep
      their "cobalt_" prefix, and any description, store page or
      announcement of a Derivative must state that it is based on Project
      Cobalt and link to https://github.com/Project-Cobalt-FiveM.

   d. Same license. A Derivative is covered by this license in full. You may
      not add terms that take away any of the rights in section 2 or relax
      any condition in section 3.

   e. Keep the notices. Keep this license file, the copyright notice above
      and any credit notices in the Software in every copy you share.

4. Other people's code

   Parts of Project Cobalt are separate projects under their own licenses,
